From: Jiahao Xu <xujiahao@cmss.chinamobile.com>
To: Borislav Petkov <bp@alien8.de>, Tony Luck <tony.luck@intel.com>
Cc: Qiuxu Zhuo <qzhuo@nvidia.com>, linux-edac@vger.kernel.org,
    linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org
Subject: [PATCH] EDAC: enlarge the DIMM label buffer so the widest format fits

The DIMM labels are assembled with snprintf() into
label[EDAC_MC_LABEL_LEN + 1], a 32-byte buffer, with formats such as
"CPU_SrcID#%u_MC#%u_Chan#%u_DIMM#%u" in skx_common.c and
"CPU_SrcID#%u_Ha#%u_Chan#%u_DIMM#%u" in sb_edac.c.

The compiler cannot see that the source ids come from 3-bit PCI
configuration space fields (skx_get_src_id() masks bits 12..14) and
that the channel and slot indices are small, so it computes a worst
case of 34 characters plus the terminator, one byte more than the
buffer holds, and reports it in a W=1 build:

  drivers/edac/skx_common.c:790:87: warning: '_DIMM#' directive output
    may be truncated writing 6 bytes into a region of size between 0
    and 9 [-Wformat-truncation=]
  drivers/edac/skx_common.c:839:79: warning: '_DIMM#' directive output
    may be truncated writing 6 bytes into a region of size between 0
    and 9 [-Wformat-truncation=]
  drivers/edac/sb_edac.c:1670:85: warning: 'snprintf' output may be
    truncated before the last format character [-Wformat-truncation=]

The labels fit in practice, but the buffer is one byte short of what
the compiler is allowed to assume, so raise EDAC_MC_LABEL_LEN to 34.
The label array of struct edac_raw_error_desc and the stack buffers of
the three drivers that size them with this constant grow by the same
three bytes.

No functional change.

Signed-off-by: Jiahao Xu <xujiahao@cmss.chinamobile.com>
---
 include/linux/edac.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/include/linux/edac.h b/include/linux/edac.h
index f7a8218f9..f4c0a9613 100644
--- a/include/linux/edac.h
+++ b/include/linux/edac.h
@@ -45,7 +45,7 @@ static inline void opstate_init(void)
 }
 
 /* Max length of a DIMM label*/
-#define EDAC_MC_LABEL_LEN	31
+#define EDAC_MC_LABEL_LEN	34
 
 /* Maximum size of the location string */
 #define LOCATION_SIZE 256
